## SEVERITY / VERDICT (round 1's, plus)
Blocker: round 1's list, and **any round-1 Blocker still open or regressed**; a canary/personal-data item in the scrubbed payload on either app (resource attribute, metric attribute, exception frame/name, log scope, first path segment, instance id included); a web host other than ingestion and `settings.sdk.monitor.azure.com` (169.254.*, Statsbeat host); a readable resource string refused by the new check; an existing expectation edited beyond the ruled list; an ignore line wider than one fingerprint; a path outside the 35. Major: a surviving mutant; a dead canary; a control row red once; a false README statement (incl. OneSettings); a B431 Major still open. Minor/Note as round 1. Overall **GO** · **GO WITH FINDINGS** · **NO GO**. **Round-2 rule: NO GO on the same class as round 1 = the work STOPS and goes to the product owner as a card (Tuesday writes it); do not suggest a round 3.**
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B436 (round 2 of 2): <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 39d4d1a (EQ <35 paths, 17 commits, outside partition 0, existing edits n of n ruled> · regression <B431-1..10: closed n, open n, regressed n> · privacy <canaries planted n, found scrubbed n, stock control n, dead n, extra hunted n, found n; both apps y/n> · allow-list <derived y/n, leaks n> · outbound <api hosts n, web hosts n (OneSettings only y/n), README true y/n> · inert <no string / bad strings / dead receiver ok y/n; template string accepted y/n> · exemption <rows n of n> · gitleaks <ignore lines 8 y/n, history rc, canary rc, new-commit rc> · suites <api n/n x3, control rows 14/14 x3, web n/n, infra n/n, lost 0, build rc> · mutants <n of 11+ red, survivors> · class hunt <places n, new instances n> · deps <audit rc> · cost <ok y/n> · visible words 0 · CI/CodeQL <state>)`. Then: Step 0 · REFUSE counts · PINS (start, mid, verdict: branch beside every sha) · instrument versions and load per heavy start · REGRESSION table · checks 1-8 · findings `B436-n` (severity, `path:line` at the sha, instrument, FAIL met, evidence class, fix-shape in prose) · **FOR TUESDAY** (PR only on GO/GWF; the card if NO GO; Phase B prerequisites; the cost line) · FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes and trees left · **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B436 b429/telemetry-224 @ 39d4d1a on main <sha7>: telemetry 224 round 2 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (no PR yet: CodeQL not run)` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict; CI suffix as measured) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

